            <ArticleTitle>In trans hydrolysis of carrier protein-bound acyl intermediates by CitA during citrinin biosynthesis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>50-53</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7cc07079a</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Polyketide synthases (PKSs) have several known editing mechanisms to ensure that non-productive intermediates are removed from the acyl carrier protein (ACP). We demonstrate that CitA, a putative hydrolase in the citrinin biosynthetic gene cluster, removes ACP-bound acyl intermediates. We propose that it serves an editing role in trans.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
